	"bugClass": {
		"id": "launch-policy-drift",
		"title": "Native launch or retry rebuilds the preview policy and loses effective settings",
		"cause": "A native entry point independently assembles the policy used to start a run. That assembly can omit routing settings, configured limits or finished-run history, or apply different rules for choosing the project working directory or resolving a retired model.",
		"criteria": "Trace the same project settings and run history through preview and through a native launch or retry to the execution boundary. Classify a site if its separate policy assembly causes any one difference: routing configuration is lost, a configured run limit is replaced or omitted, finished runs are missing from a history-dependent decision, the working directory violates project policy, or a retired model identifier reaches execution without the normalization used by preview. A difference on either launch or retry is sufficient.",
